# L §2.4 Expressions (tally 2.1.6, issue #81): a keyword before ( keeps its space, written: not(p and q) and
# diff(x) print not (p and q) and diff (x), as refcore and the engine printed them (M0's format vectors of diff
# texts keep their hashes). A twin: it passes on tally 2.1.5 too.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def e: bool = not(p and q)

ask qd: diff(x) in s1 against m law 2026-06-30
=== expect
--- m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def e: bool = not (p and q)

ask qd: diff (x) in s1 against m law 2026-06-30
sha256 ...
